<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rionegro Convention</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1863</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rionegro">Rionegro</a> Convention was the constituent assembly that met at Rionegro, Antioquia, in 1863 after the Liberal victory in the Colombian civil war of 1860–1862. Dominated by radical Liberals, it adopted the Constitution of 1863, which created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Colombia, a loose federation of nine sovereign states with a weak central government and broad civil liberties, lasting until 1886.</p></div>
